// Model number -> model entry, read by `cargo xtask codegen` and checked by
// `python3 control_tables/check_tables.py`.
//
// family:  the Cargo feature that compiles the model in: "ax", "mx", "rx",
//          "x-series", "y-series" or "pro".
// name:    the product name on the model's e-Manual page.
// also:    optional; other products sold under the same model number.
// p1:      the control tables (file stems in this directory) the model uses on
//          a Protocol 1.0 bus, in firmware order. Each applies from `from_fw`
//          up to the next item's `from_fw`; the first `from_fw` is 0 and they
//          strictly increase. Every table listed here has P1 in its `protocols`.
// p2:      the same for a Protocol 2.0 bus (tables with P2 in `protocols`).
//          A model has `p1`, `p2` or both. One file may sit in both lists of
//          its number, never under two numbers.
// default: P2, present exactly when both `p1` and `p2` exist.
// tables:  legacy list read by today's codegen; in this release it equals the
//          default list (or the only list). It is removed once codegen reads
//          `p1` and `p2`.
//
// not_mapped: every table file that no model number points to, with the
//          reason: `NoModelNumber` (its page gives no number) or
//          `SameNumberAs(n)` (its page gives number n, already in `models`).
//          A table is never left out of `models` for being unverified.
(
  models: {
    12: (family: "ax", name: "AX-12A", p1: [(from_fw: 0, file: "ax_12a")], tables: [(from_fw: 0, file: "ax_12a")]),
